WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:06.130
Luffy's bounty will surpass Roger at the end
of the story and I will prove it to you with

00:00:06.130 --> 00:00:07.130
math.

00:00:07.130 --> 00:00:13.469
I've always found bounties pretty irrelevant
in one piece, until recently, when I suddenly

00:00:13.469 --> 00:00:21.660
changed my mind about them.

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:26.340
Bounties actually serve a number of purposes
in the story, it's just that I really hate

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:29.359
80% of the toxic power-scaling among fans.

00:00:29.359 --> 00:00:32.520
And a lot of them bring up bounties.

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:38.039
So I guess, by default, I got annoyed with
the idea and kind of threw it aside as a nice

00:00:38.039 --> 00:00:40.410
little gadget Oda introduced.

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:44.969
However I was watching a really interesting
docu on pirates the other night when I couldn't

00:00:44.969 --> 00:00:50.260
sleep, and it sort of hit me that bounties
were a very real and important thing, heck

00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:52.460
still are in some places on earth.

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:57.559
I mean I knew that, but having it presented
in that way really had me change my mind.

00:00:57.559 --> 00:01:02.359
Hi my name is Manu, my favorite bounty is
the one filled with coconut cream, fuck that's

00:01:02.359 --> 00:01:06.229
delicious, and today I'm going to explain
how bounties in One Piece work, my personal

00:01:06.229 --> 00:01:10.320
prediction for the straw hats final bounties
and at the end of this video I will show you

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:16.060
how Luffy's bounties have helped to make one
piece great.

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:19.460
A bounty is actually a pretty smart system
in itself.

00:01:19.460 --> 00:01:23.320
Here's the deal: Imagine a government that
has a problem on a large scale.

00:01:23.320 --> 00:01:28.229
A problem so big and common that the government
alone can't handle it.

00:01:28.229 --> 00:01:32.030
So they offer money to anyone who is willing
to help.

00:01:32.030 --> 00:01:36.010
So a bounty can be on people or animals or
really anything else.

00:01:36.010 --> 00:01:39.240
You can earn money by locating, capturing
or killing.

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:44.460
In one piece, the problem the government is
dealing with are pirates, because all pirates

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:48.159
are evil, and not because they fucked over
the entire world.

00:01:48.159 --> 00:01:52.630
Oh but actually it turns out there is also
bounties on revolutionaries.

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:57.679
So in One Piece, whether or not you get a
bounty is not determined by how dangerous

00:01:57.679 --> 00:02:02.579
you are to the people, but how dangerous you
are to the rule of the world government itself.

00:02:02.579 --> 00:02:09.200
I think a big mistake some people make, not
you I know, but some people, is taking the

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:11.530
bounty system as a system for power scaling.

00:02:11.530 --> 00:02:15.580
In other words, the higher a bounty, the stronger
the person.

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:16.620
That's wrong.

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:17.620
Sorry.

00:02:17.620 --> 00:02:19.180
Of course power plays a role.

00:02:19.180 --> 00:02:20.610
I'm not denying that.

00:02:20.610 --> 00:02:25.210
Logically by becoming powerful, you potentially
pose a bigger threat.

00:02:25.210 --> 00:02:36.760
And even pirates themselves expect a certain
level of power from someone with a high bounty.

00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:40.290
[] However the fact that dragon is the most
wanted man in the world, as I explained in

00:02:40.290 --> 00:02:47.269
his analysis video, is because he is a powerful
person actively working to tear down the established

00:02:47.269 --> 00:02:48.330
world order.

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:52.790
Not because he's stronger than Kaido or Whitebeard
- probably, right?

00:02:52.790 --> 00:02:53.790
Right??

00:02:53.790 --> 00:02:54.790
Yeah.

00:02:54.790 --> 00:02:55.790
Right?

00:02:55.790 --> 00:03:00.660
Similarly, before the time-skip, kid's bounty
was larger than luffy's because he went around

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:06.069
killing and pillaging, unlike Luffy, who's
mostly just hanging out and making friends

00:03:06.069 --> 00:03:07.500
wherever he goes.

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:09.790
Oda actually confirmed this in an SBS.

00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:15.610
He also noted, that within a crew, the captain's
bounties always increases more than the crew

00:03:15.610 --> 00:03:19.629
members' even if the power difference isn't
that big.

00:03:19.629 --> 00:03:23.689
There are a few interesting details to the
bounty system.

00:03:23.689 --> 00:03:29.010
Obtaining a bounty in the first place, basically
means you are officially a criminal in the

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:30.010
government's eyes.

00:03:30.010 --> 00:03:35.370
I think we tend to forget this a bunch, but
these posters actually say dead or alive.

00:03:35.370 --> 00:03:38.010
Which is pretty wild, no?

00:03:38.010 --> 00:03:44.040
Once you get a bounty, anyone, ANYONE can
come and just shoot you and it's completely

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:45.040
legal.

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:49.670
Which is really fucked up when you think about
examples like little robin, who got her bounty

00:03:49.670 --> 00:03:51.599
for being the last survivor of Ohara.

00:03:51.599 --> 00:04:01.239
A 
little girl with no human rights, if you can

00:04:01.239 --> 00:04:04.599
call it human rights what the world government
is pretending to protect.

00:04:04.599 --> 00:04:10.280
And of course in just a bit we will look at
Robin's final bounty in the story.

00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:15.829
The bounties themselves can be found in bars,
public places and marine buildings.

00:04:15.829 --> 00:04:20.800
They serve to warn common citizens of dangerous
criminals, detain these people from entering

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:26.610
a city and at the same time incentivize bounty
hunters, such as Zoro used to be, to go after

00:04:26.610 --> 00:04:37.420
these people and earn a living from turning
them in or killing them.

00:04:37.420 --> 00:04:42.010
Even though he never discussed it, I'm pretty
sure Oda got inspiration for this system from

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:47.880
his love for western, the bounties on real
world pirates as well as the pictures of wanted

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:50.630
criminals in Japanese police stations.

00:04:50.630 --> 00:04:54.770
They remind me a lot of these wanted posters
whenever I see them.

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:58.950
Funnily enough however, even though bounties
are supposed to be something bad and deter

00:04:58.950 --> 00:05:03.750
bad people from doing bad things, in the world
of one piece, where the government is as corrupt,

00:05:03.750 --> 00:05:13.340
hypocritical and unfair as it gets, pirates
actually take a lot of pride in their bounty.

00:05:13.340 --> 00:05:21.360
It serves as a sort of proof of achievement,
where they get their pirate grades at the

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:23.420
end of the year.

00:05:23.420 --> 00:05:30.950
While portrayed in a funny way, as you know,
one piece has a very dark sub-tone.

00:05:30.950 --> 00:05:36.620
And so for me the fact that there are so many
pirates in this world, forming their own societies

00:05:36.620 --> 00:05:42.350
and groups shows us how broken the system
here really is.

00:05:42.350 --> 00:05:47.700
Many of the people we meet, only became pirates,
because all over the world people live in

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:51.810
desperation, war and hardship, while the rich
and powerful play god.

00:05:51.810 --> 00:05:57.090
Now however, I want to give off my own predictions
for each of the straw hats' final bounties.

00:05:57.090 --> 00:05:58.090
-

00:05:58.090 --> 00:06:02.320
Luckily, I have a lot I can work with, now
that we finally know some of the biggest bounties

00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:03.320
in the story.

00:06:03.320 --> 00:06:13.000
The largest bounty so far belongs of course
to the pirate king himself.

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:19.530
That's about 5 million dollars, which is a
lot of money, but enough to risk your life

00:06:19.530 --> 00:06:22.960
against one of the strongest people in the
world?

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:31.030
Eaahhh I'd probably pass and go for, like
i dunno 50 buggies or something.

00:06:31.030 --> 00:06:36.050
We actually do know the bounty for all the
yonko as well as most of the commanders.

00:06:36.050 --> 00:06:41.270
This already gives us a pretty nice range
of where things are heading.

00:06:41.270 --> 00:06:46.940
Two bounties I wish I knew for this are that
of dragon and rocks.

00:06:46.940 --> 00:06:53.150
How big is the bounty on the head of the most
wanted criminal, who plans to topple the government?

00:06:53.150 --> 00:06:58.220
And how much for rocks, the captain of the
most notorious pirate crew?

00:06:58.220 --> 00:07:00.060
But let's work with what we get.

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:01.060
*drops cup*

00:07:01.060 --> 00:07:02.060
Was the cup empty?

00:07:02.060 --> 00:07:04.650
Will my bounty predictions be completely off?

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:08.770
Am I gonna lose all sponsorships because this
transition is so weird?

00:07:08.770 --> 00:07:12.150
Find out right after you subscribe you filthy
coward.

00:07:12.150 --> 00:07:13.810
But first a word from our sponsor.

00:07:13.810 --> 00:07:16.990
A: Jesus, and there they said the rainforests
are dying.

00:07:16.990 --> 00:07:17.990
B: Who are you?

00:07:17.990 --> 00:07:22.640
A: You know, I know we're in Japan my friend,
but this is taking cultural appropriation

00:07:22.640 --> 00:07:23.640
too far.

00:07:23.640 --> 00:07:25.949
B: how did you get into my apartment?

00:07:25.949 --> 00:07:26.949
- what?

00:07:26.949 --> 00:07:31.690
A: I'm salesman Manu, you are live in your
own video right now and I have just the thing

00:07:31.690 --> 00:07:32.690
for you.

